Description: Estimates expected case counts for each district and month
    using Bayesian spatial and temporal models fitted with INLA. The
    surveillance performance index (SPI) compares observed and expected
    counts and, by default, divides each district ratio by the national
    ratio for the same period. Credible intervals describe uncertainty in
    expected counts. An annual SPI can also be calculated from earlier
    reporting without INLA or district boundaries.
    Functions check inputs, compare SPI with conventional reporting targets,
    and produce tables, maps, and district reports for surveillance review.
    Designed for acute flaccid paralysis (AFP) surveillance, with support
    for other case-based surveillance data.
